      },
      "BlobV1": {
        "type": "string",
        "format": "byte",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 1048576,
        "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9+/]+={0,2}$",
        "title": "BlobV1",
        "description": "Opaque client-encrypted blob (base64). Layout: [1-byte version][12-byte IV][ciphertext+16-byte GCM tag]. AES-GCM uses Additional Authenticated Data (AAD) built as UTF8(NFC(user_id)) + 0x1F + UTF8(NFC(item_id)) + 0x1F + UTF8(NFC(service_name)) in the exact field order user_id, item_id, service_name. Example: AAD = UTF8(NFC('user')) + 0x1F + UTF8(NFC('item')) + 0x1F + UTF8(NFC('service')). The server treats this as opaque bytes and never decrypts it."
      },
